WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.840
Привет, Фрэнс!

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.700
Welcome to привет, русский, Episode 54, for 8 July, 2026.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:09.580
I'm Olya, and we've got some great Russian words to learn today.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.180
Поехали, let's go!

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:17.120
Our word of the day is «семья» — «семья» — «семья».

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.860
It sounds like seminar, but it means the people you gather with every day.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.080
This word helps us talk about the heart of a home.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.780
Listen to it in a sentence.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.340
Это моя семья, that means this is my family.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.360
Now repeat after me, «семья» — «семья».

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.400
Let's meet the people inside a семья.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.180
The first is «мама», «матомыл», it means «month over month».

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:44.200
Моя мама любит читать, that means my month over month loves to read.

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:51.320
Repeat after me, «mama», «mama», «mama» sounds exactly like the English word «mama».

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.340
Both words come from the very first sounds babies make all over the world.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:01.100
This word started as a natural baby sound and settled into Russian with almost no change.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.980
Next time you hear «мама», remember it is cousins with Russian «мама».

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:08.980
Next comes «папа», «пэ» — «пэ», it means dead.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.800
Папа работает, that means dead is working.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:17.140
Say it with me, «папа», «папа», «пап» sounds exactly like English «папа».

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:20.560
In some languages, the same sound can mean something else entirely.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:25.400
Now we add a sibling, «брат» — «брат», it means «brother».

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.840
У меня есть «брат», that means I have a brother.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:33.180
Repeat after me, «брат» — «брат», «брат», «брат» sounds like the English word «брат».

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.460
It actually means the helpful sibling instead.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:40.720
Here is another sibling, «систра», «сестра», it means «систра».

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.840
Моя «сестра» играет, that means my sister is playing.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:48.080
«Трэд» — «сестра» — «сестра» — «сестра» — «бигинствует» — «сест»,

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:49.240
like the English sister.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:52.220
The ending — «тра» — «комплейс» — «доворт».

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:56.760
We also have «бабушка», «бэп» — «ушка», it means «grandmother».

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.640
«Бабушка» — «печет пироги», that means «grandma big spice».

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.840
Repeat after me, «бабушка», «бабушка» — «бабушка»

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.680
из-за фейма «сраженвард» for grandmother.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:08.640
Say it with a smile to remember it easily.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.780
Мить дедушка, детьушка, it means «grandfather».

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.780
Дедушка рассказывает истории.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.320
That means «grandpotel stories».

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.880
Say it slowly, «дедушка» — «дедушка», «дедушка» — «дедушка».

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.380
Starts with that like that.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.400
The ending — «ушка» — «терзат» into grandfather.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:30.780
One more family member is «дочь», «дочь — it means daughter».

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:34.060
Моя «дочь» любит кошку, that means my daughter loves the cat.

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:38.140
Repeat after me, «дочь» — «дочь» — «дочь» — раем с водой.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.460
It brings to mind the girl who helps the family rise with joy.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.080
In Russian, family words often change their ending to show my or your.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.640
We add a or ya for my.

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:51.380
My mom means my month over months.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.360
My papa means my dad.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.660
My sister means my sister.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:00.540
In this uses my too, but Russian makes the ending much the person.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:05.700
In Russia, Babushka often helps raise grandchildren and cook big Sunday meals.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:09.220
Families gather around the table for long talks and tea.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.740
This makes Simya feel like the center of daily life.

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:16.940
For kids, dry your Simya and label each person with the new words.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:18.620
Then say them out loud.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.280
For adults, introduce your family using my or my.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:24.720
Remember Dom from a few lessons ago.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:27.300
That is the house where your Simya lives.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.460
Want to know a secret about one of today's words?

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:35.580
The Russian word «Mama» and the English word «Mama» are actually the same word.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:41.680
This word travelled through ancient languages and stayed almost unchanged in both Russian and English.

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:47.220
That connection helps you remember it forever — «Молодец», that means well done.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:52.900
Remember every expert started as a beginner, practicing today's words out loud,

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.320
even just once, and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:58.280
See you next time, пока!

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.660
That's Russian for «Бай».

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:05.900
And if you'd rather watch them this time, find us on YouTube at NERA-RU, links in the show notes.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:12.220
This is the end of the episode of the Russian word «Mama» and the English word «M».
